## Core concepts
- [What is an AI agent](https://www.make.com/blog/what-is-an-ai-agent): Definition of an AI agent, how it differs from a scripted automation, and what it needs to act reliably.
- [What is agentic AI](https://www.make.com/blog/what-is-agentic-ai): The perceive–reason–act–learn loop, where autonomy helps, and where it introduces risk.
- [AI agents vs. agentic automation](https://www.make.com/blog/the-difference-between-ai-agents-and-agentic-automation): Why the two terms are not interchangeable, and what changes operationally when you move from one to the other.
- [What is AI automation](https://www.make.com/blog/what-is-ai-automation): Where AI models fit inside an automated workflow, and which steps should stay deterministic.
- [Deterministic vs. non-deterministic automation](https://www.make.com/blog/the-rise-of-nondeterministic-automation): The tradeoffs between predictable, fixed workflows and adaptive ones, and how to combine both in a single system.
- [What is MCP and the Make MCP server](https://www.make.com/blog/model-context-protocol-mcp-server): How the Model Context Protocol exposes Make scenarios as tools to an external AI agent, without hosting infrastructure or writing API endpoints.
- [MCP client](https://www.make.com/blog/mcp-client): The inverse direction — letting a Make scenario or agent call MCP tools hosted outside Make.
- [What is no-code automation](https://www.make.com/blog/no-code-automation): Definition, tradeoffs, and how visual builders compare to text-based and code-first tools.
- [What is workflow automation](https://www.make.com/blog/workflow-automation): Core vocabulary — triggers, actions, branching, aggregation — with a worked example.
- [What is a visual workflow](https://www.make.com/blog/visual-workflows): Why Make represents logic as a canvas rather than a list of steps, and what that changes for debugging.
- [What is an API integration](https://www.make.com/blog/what-is-api-integration): How API integrations work and how to build one without a prebuilt connector.
- [What are webhooks](https://www.make.com/blog/what-are-webhooks): How webhooks deliver events in real time and how to receive them in a scenario.
- [Webhooks vs. APIs](https://www.make.com/blog/webhook-vs-api): Push vs. pull, and which one to reach for in a given trigger design.
- [Connecting to anything with an API](https://www.make.com/blog/connect-to-anything-with-an-api): Using HTTP modules or a custom app when no prebuilt connector exists.
- [Business process automation](https://www.make.com/blog/business-process-automation-guide): Identifying, scoping, and sequencing processes worth automating.

